 "notes": "Combined envelope of \u03bdE3/\u03bdE2 and \u03bdE3/\u03bdSr optical clock comparison limits. Extracted from Figure 4 (vector curves in filled regions). Paper uses \u03c1_DM \u2248 0.4 GeV/cm\u00b3. Coupling d_e defined via L \u2283 (d_e/4\u03bc\u2080) \u03c6 F_\u03bc\u03bd F^\u03bc\u03bd in Lagrangian. Paper notes that for masses below ~10^-22 eV, the assumption that the field makes up all dark matter needs to be relaxed. \u03bdE3/\u03bdSr is more stringent above 10^-20 eV; \u03bdE3/\u03bdE2 better below that mass. Combined results show >order of magnitude improvement over previous bounds for mid-10^-23 to mid-10^-18 eV.",
